<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office for the Wednesday-to-Sunday Thanksgiving holiday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data is due Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) 101 Dalmatians .............. $46.0 million</p>
<p>    2 (1) Star Trek: First Contact .... $23.4 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Space Jam ................... $17.9 million</p>
<p>    4 (3) Ransom ...................... $17.6 million</p>
<p>    5 (4) Jingle All the Way .......... $17.5 million</p>
<p>    6 (5) The Mirror Has Two Faces ....  $8.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (8) The English Patient .........  $5.9 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) Set It Off ..................  $4.6 million</p>
<p>    9 (7) Romeo &amp; Juliet ..............  $3.5 million</p>
<p>   10 (9) Sleepers ..................... $1.5 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Rank last week in parentheses.</p>
<p>&quot;101&quot; Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;Ransom&quot; released by Walt Disney Co., &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc., &quot;Space Jam&quot; and &quot;Sleepers&quot; by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc., &quot;Jingle All The Way&quot; and &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; released by Sony Corp. and &quot;The English Patient&quot; by Disney's Miramax Films. &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
